<title>SWEDEN: Skandia open for financial deal - paper.</title>
<headline>Skandia open for financial deal - paper.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurer Skandia could be interested in a new financial deal after losing its planned bride, mortgage lender Stadshypotek, to Handelsbanken, daily Finanstidningen said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We hold the door open for other business opportunities in the financial sector in the Nordic region,&quot; Bjorn Wolrath, Skandia's former chief executive who still is active within the group, was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>&quot;A merger with an insurance company means a large rationalisation potential while a merger with a bank gives access to the bank's customer basis and distribution network,&quot; he told the newspaper.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
